{"title":"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 19","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Two angles of an isosceles triangle measure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31adfcb608f857dff15cc5fa7ea0c327e8dc65ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a66181795ab222ad9ff38cb534dead38e5a47de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />. What is the sum of the three possible values of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/a/75a67dcdec7358fa1076cab47e81b0dfdcb31399.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\   95    \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\    125   \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\    140   \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\    165   \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\     180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"430\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are 3 cases: where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a66181795ab222ad9ff38cb534dead38e5a47de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> is a base angle with the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31adfcb608f857dff15cc5fa7ea0c327e8dc65ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> as the other angle, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a66181795ab222ad9ff38cb534dead38e5a47de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> is a base angle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31adfcb608f857dff15cc5fa7ea0c327e8dc65ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> as the vertex angle, and where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a66181795ab222ad9ff38cb534dead38e5a47de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> is the vertex angle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31adfcb608f857dff15cc5fa7ea0c327e8dc65ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> as a base angle.\n</p><p>Case 1: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a66181795ab222ad9ff38cb534dead38e5a47de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> is a base angle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31adfcb608f857dff15cc5fa7ea0c327e8dc65ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> as the other angle:\nHere, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/9/5/295fd8a2ce69bd8e06fb88a96d7184e238a72fc6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=70$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />, since base angles are congruent.\n</p><p>Case 2: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a66181795ab222ad9ff38cb534dead38e5a47de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> is a base angle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31adfcb608f857dff15cc5fa7ea0c327e8dc65ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> as the vertex angle:\nHere, the 2 base angles are both <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a66181795ab222ad9ff38cb534dead38e5a47de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" />, so we can use the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/8/65861878520769d4a2650181ad2da744adfb9dcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2x+70=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"14\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96a42969703b8f5e19032dd4bd83c9e4522527c4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=55$\" width=\"52\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>Case 3: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/6/7a66181795ab222ad9ff38cb534dead38e5a47de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"15\" /> is the vertex angle with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31adfcb608f857dff15cc5fa7ea0c327e8dc65ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" /> as a base angle:\nHere, both base angles are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/a/31adfcb608f857dff15cc5fa7ea0c327e8dc65ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"28\" height=\"15\" />, since base angles are congruent. Thus, we can use the equation <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/a/b/eab97395010d234ac7edb7aa8a7b1716c1b766a3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+140=180$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"110\" height=\"14\" />, which simplifies to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/8/5/b858aee871cc6fe6149cf70fbb27f55339ad7556.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=40$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Adding up all the cases, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/8/c789550852b991786d665c599744ab42eed51840.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$70+55+40=165$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"149\" height=\"14\" />, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/1/e/31ea92b693bbf1509a0d56a828c4c590d51a7aaf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\    165}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"74\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/FDgcLW4frg8?t=902\">https://youtu.be/FDgcLW4frg8?t=902</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p><p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EO3DphZAlDY\">https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=EO3DphZAlDY</a>   ~David\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_2\">Video Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/iB0dcpVREE8\">https://youtu.be/iB0dcpVREE8</a> Soo, DRMS, NM\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_19&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8\" title=\"2009 AMC 8\">2009 AMC 8</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Answer_Key\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=42&amp;year=2009\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_18\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 18\">Problem 18</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 20\">Problem 20</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2009 AMC 8 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2009_AMC_8_Prob